{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:UGB.UnitalGroebner.unital_groebner_decomposition","@type":"LeanModule","name":"UGB.UnitalGroebner.unital_groebner_decomposition","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Basic","lean:module:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Flatness"],"declarations":1,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.UnitalGroebner.unital_groebner_decomposition","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.UnitalGroebner.unital_groebner_decomposition","kind":"theorem","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/UnitalGroebner/unital_groebner_decomposition.lean#L60-L92","doc":"**Free-module decomposition — `Õ(G)`-component + flatness.**\n\nFor a Gröbner–Shirshov basis `sys`, every element `f` reduces to a\nnormal form (the `Õ(G)`-summand of `f` in `A = I ⊕ Õ(G)`), and the\ndeformed/graded Hilbert functions agree (`isFlat`).\n\nThe conclusion is a **concrete conjunction**: a `ReducesToNF`\nexistential over `AlgElement` together with an `isFlat` equality of\nHilbert functions — substantive content the former `holds : Prop`\nlacked. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:thm:unital-groebner-decomposition","label":"thm:unital-groebner-decomposition","md":"unital-groebner-bases/unital-groebner-bases-chapter/main-theorem.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}